  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">PROMOTING LIVELIHOODS, AGRICULTURE, NUTRITION AND NATURAL RESOURCES (PLANN)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Promoting Livelihoods, Agriculture, Nutrition and Natural Resources (PLANN), is a one-year project designed to support 40 rural communities across 4 chiefdoms in the Kailahun district. Improve food security, livelihoods and the nutritional status of vulnerable groups particularly women, children and adolescent girls, through tested and proven integrated approaches such as nutrition sensitive agriculture, linking agriculture and natural resource management (LANN) and the gender model family (GMF).</narrative>
  </description>
